{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit\/gettingstarted"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/TimeAndObservers"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"AstronomyKit provides a type-safe Swift interface for astronomical calculations. This article walks you through installation and your first calculations.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Installation","anchor":"Installation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add AstronomyKit to your Swift package:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["dependencies: [","    .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/AstronomyKit\", from: \"4.0.0\")","]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Or in Xcode: ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"File → Add Package Dependencies","type":"text"}]},{"text":" and enter the repository URL.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Your First Calculations","anchor":"Your-First-Calculations"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Import the Package","anchor":"Import-the-Package"},{"code":["import AstronomyKit"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Set Up Your Observer Location","anchor":"Set-Up-Your-Observer-Location"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Most astronomical calculations require an observer location on Earth:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ New York City","let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7128, longitude: -74.0060)","","\/\/ With elevation (in meters)","let denver = Observer(latitude: 39.7392, longitude: -104.9903, height: 1609)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Get the Current Time","anchor":"Get-the-Current-Time"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"AstronomyKit uses ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for all time-based calculations:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Current time","let now = AstroTime.now","","\/\/ From a specific date","let newYear = AstroTime(year: 2025, month: 1, day: 1, hour: 12)","","\/\/ From Foundation Date","let fromDate = AstroTime(Date())"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Calculate a Position","anchor":"Calculate-a-Position"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Find where a celestial body appears in your sky:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Mars in the local sky","let mars = try CelestialBody.mars.horizon(at: .now, from: observer)","print(\"Altitude: \\(mars.altitude)°\")     \/\/ Height above horizon","print(\"Direction: \\(mars.compassDirection)\")  \/\/ N, NE, E, etc."],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Find the Moon Phase","anchor":"Find-the-Moon-Phase"},{"code":["let angle = try Moon.phaseAngle(at: .now)","print(\"\\(Moon.emoji(for: angle)) \\(Moon.phaseName(for: angle))\")","\/\/ Output: 🌔 Waxing Gibbous"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Get Rise and Set Times","anchor":"Get-Rise-and-Set-Times"},{"code":["if let sunrise = try CelestialBody.sun.riseTime(after: .now, from: observer) {","    print(\"Sunrise: \\(sunrise.date)\")","}","","if let sunset = try CelestialBody.sun.setTime(after: .now, from: observer) {","    print(\"Sunset: \\(sunset.date)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Error Handling","anchor":"Error-Handling"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All potentially failing calculations throw ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstronomyError","type":"ref